### Explored Factors

#### Relative Momentum Volatility-Scaled Variants

Tested several interpretable specifications using lagged cross-sectional relative momentum divided by asset-specific realized volatility:

\[
F_t =
\frac{R_{n,t}-\operatorname{median}(R_{n,t})}
{\sigma_{v,t}}
\]

where \(R_n\) is the \(n\)-session return and \(\sigma_v\) is rolling daily-return volatility.

Variants included:

- 5-day momentum / 20-day volatility
- 5-day momentum / 40-day volatility
- 10-day momentum / 20-day volatility
- 15-day momentum / 20-day volatility
- 15-day momentum / 40-day volatility
- 20-day momentum / 40-day volatility
- 20-day momentum / 60-day volatility
- 30-day momentum / 60-day volatility
- 10-day momentum / 40-day volatility evaluated at multiple forward horizons

The 15-day momentum / 20-day volatility specification was selected because it passed the required daily admission gates with strong historical stability.

