### Explored Factors

#### Volatility-Scaled Return Acceleration

Tested a lagged acceleration factor measuring recent 15-session return pace relative to the average pace implied by the preceding 60 sessions:

\[
F_t =
\operatorname{shift}_1\left[
\frac{R_{15,t} - R_{60,t}/4}{\sigma_{30,t}}
\right]
\]

The factor is positive when recent momentum is strengthening relative to the longer-term trend and negative when momentum is decelerating. Volatility normalization improves comparability across assets, while the one-day lag prevents look-ahead.

