### Explored Factors

#### Dispersion-Conditioned Momentum

Construction:

\[
F_t =
\operatorname{shift}\left[
\frac{R_{20,t}}{\sigma_{60,t}\sqrt{20}}
\left(0.5+B_{20,t}\right)
D_t
,1\right]
\]

where:

- \(R_{20}\) is 20-day momentum;
- \(\sigma_{60}\) is 60-day realized volatility;
- \(B_{20}\) is the cross-asset fraction of positive returns over 20 sessions;
- \(D_t\) is 20-day cross-asset return dispersion relative to its 120-day median, clipped to \([0.5,1.5]\);
- The complete signal is lagged one session.

The factor was intended to emphasize momentum when cross-asset dispersion and directional breadth supported differentiation among assets.

