#### Downside-Risk-Adjusted Medium-Term Trend

Construction:

\[
F_t =
\frac{R_{20,t-1}}
{\sqrt{20}\sqrt{\operatorname{mean}_{60}
\left(\min(R_{1},0)^2\right)}}
\]

The factor ranks assets by their lagged 20-session return, scaled by downside deviation estimated over the preceding 60 sessions. It favors persistent positive trends with lower downside risk. All inputs are lagged one session to avoid look-ahead bias.

