The small 15-asset universe was used without imposing an instrument-count minimum beyond the required eight valid instruments per date. Results covered more than 1,600 daily cross-sectional observations, with approximately 14.5 valid instruments per date on average. Despite broad date coverage, both factors exhibited persistently adverse predictive signs.

