The effective factor library remains unchanged. Existing effective factors include risk-adjusted momentum, volatility-state momentum, trend consistency, breadth, dispersion/stress reversal, range-efficiency, and related validated signals. The newly tested volume-surprise and recovery factors are not effective.

### Plans

- Investigate whether volume information is more useful as a confirmation filter for existing momentum or reversal factors rather than as a standalone alpha signal.
- Test conditional factors activated only during high cross-asset dispersion or macro stress, while avoiding duplication with existing VIX- and dispersion-conditioned reversal factors.
- Continue prioritizing low-turnover signals with stable sign across 2025–2027, since both new candidates showed negative recent-regime performance.
- Revalidate older effective factors as they approach their three-month review window.

