### Explored Factor

**Volatility-contextualized 30-day trend**

\[
F_t =
\left(\frac{P_t/P_{t-30}-1}{\sigma_{20,t}\sqrt{30}}\right)
\left(\frac{\sigma_{60,t}}{\sigma_{20,t}}\right)
\]

The factor measures 30-session momentum normalized by recent volatility, then adjusts the signal upward when longer-term volatility exceeds short-term volatility. This favors persistent trends emerging within relatively compressed short-term volatility conditions.

